    "description": "Tokyo Electric Power Company Holdings, Incorporated, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the generation, transmission, distribution, and retail of electric power in Japan and internationally. It generates power through nuclear, fuel, and thermal, as well as solar, geothermal, hydro, and offshore wind power plants; and engages in the procurement, transportation, and trading of fuel. The company is also involved in the gas supply business. In addition, it provides consulting services, as well as engages in real estate rental business; Uranium mining and smelting; system development and maintenance; design and maintenance of power distribution equipment, sales and management of utility pole advertisements; back-office operations; and sales, construction, repair, leasing, electrical work and management of machinery and equipment. Further, the company is involved in investment projects; hydroelectric power generation business; storage and management; hotel and golf course management; design project; charging service, and charging network service business; and planning, proposals, design and construction related to energy conservation in new and existing buildings, and sales and installation of building equipment, etc. The company was formerly known as Tokyo Electric Power Company, Incorporated and changed its name to Tokyo Electric Power Company Holdings, Incorporated in April 2016. The company was incorporated in 1951 and is headquartered in Tokyo, Japan. Tokyo Electric Power Company Holdings, Incorporated is a subsidiary of Nuclear Damage Compensation And Decommissioning Facilitation Corporation."
